    corridors need not be contiguous
  transform:
    fill interior cells of each unblocked row corridor with green
    fill interior cells of each unblocked column corridor with green
    intersections get green; original foreground cells unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size N x N in [10, 14].
    2. Choose a border partition -- pick 2 transition points on the border loop to divide it into a red arc and a teal arc (each arc >= N cells). Fill all border cells accordingly.
    3. Choose 1-4 corridor rows (not row 0 or N-1) and 1-3 corridor columns (not col 0 or N-1). Leave their interior cells black.
    4. For non-corridor rows/columns, place interior foreground blockers so that every non-corridor row with two foreground border endpoints has at least one blocker in its interior span (and likewise for columns). Use a mix of red and teal.
    5. Ensure each color (red, teal) forms a single connected component across the whole grid. Grow blockers from same-color border regions inward via flood-fill or random walk. Retry or adjust if connectivity breaks.
    6. Verify interior foreground density is 15-30%.
    7. Input = the grid with corridors left black. Output = fill corridor interiors with green.
