spec:
  grid: 10-14 rows x 10-14 cols, square
  background: black
  colors: red (2) and teal (8) foreground; green (3) reserved for output
  border:
    every border cell is foreground (red or teal)
    border loop has exactly 2 color transitions, splitting it into two contiguous arcs
    partition style varies -- horizontal, vertical, or L-shaped (3 corners same, 1 differs)
  interior_blockers:
    each color forms exactly one 4-connected component across the full grid (border + interior)
    interior foreground density 18-27% of (H-2)x(W-2) cells
    blockers are placed to block some row/column corridors while leaving others clear
  corridors:
    row corridor = row where both border endpoints are foreground and all interior cells are black
    column corridor = column where both border endpoints are foreground and all interior cells are black
    unblocked row corridors: 1-6 [observed >= 2]
    unblocked column corridors: 1-3 [observed >= 1]
    at least 1 of each kind required (solver asserts)
    corridors need not be contiguous
  transform:
    fill interior cells of each unblocked row corridor with green
